16
00:00:42,479 --> 00:00:48,480
Could AI enabled diagnostics unlock precision medicine?

17
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:53,120
Essentially, could we use diagnostics as a vehicle to make precision medicine

18
00:00:53,159 --> 00:00:57,439
as opposed to targeted medicine a reality?

19
00:00:57,439 --> 00:01:00,839
In order to do so, you really need two things.

20
00:01:00,839 --> 00:01:05,000
You need access to vast amounts of proprietary data to train models and

21
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,599
uncover insights, and you need a distribution system to deliver those

22
00:01:08,599 --> 00:01:11,479
insights to the hands of physicians and patients.

23
00:01:11,479 --> 00:01:18,599
Most people have failed historically at having one or both of those.

24
00:01:18,599 --> 00:01:22,400
We have spent the last 10 years building both.

25
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:26,240
We've built up a data set that is now quite substantial.

26
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:29,680
And equally importantly, we built up distribution capabilities to take those

27
00:01:29,680 --> 00:01:35,320
insights and distribute them to tens of thousands of physicians across the

28
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:40,640
country reaching millions of patients to advance therapy selection.

29
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:45,760
What therapeutic path should my patient be on to advance clinical trial matching?

30
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:47,360
Is there a trial that they're eligible for and

31
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:49,640
ultimately to advance research and drug discovery?

32
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:56,319
The idea we had 10 years ago was that in order to bring AI to healthcare,

33
00:01:56,319 --> 00:01:57,400
you had to start somewhere.

34
00:01:57,400 --> 00:02:00,400
We thought you should start with diagnostics.

35
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:05,400
It's the only external data modality that physicians interact with all day long.

36
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:08,639
So you either, if you want to bring AI to the healthcare system,

37
00:02:08,639 --> 00:02:11,360
you either ask doctors to go somewhere.

38
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:17,000
You take systems like Epic and make them AI enabled.

39
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,280
Or you have to find some alternative pathway.

40
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:23,199
Given that physicians order laboratory test results and routine diagnostics when

41
00:02:23,199 --> 00:02:27,360
they make almost every major decision, we thought if you could wrap AI around

42
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:32,319
the diagnostic itself, you could kind of infuse the benefits of technology

43
00:02:32,319 --> 00:02:33,800
into healthcare.

44
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:37,920
And so the platform we built is now broadly connected to about more than

45
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:40,560
5,000 providers across the United States.

46
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:44,920
To put that in perspective, it's probably two-thirds or so of the United States

47
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:48,000
who are connected to Tempus in some way, shape, or form.

48
00:02:48,039 --> 00:02:52,599
We're either ordering our tests or using our technology to match their patients to

49
