clinical trials or close care gaps, things of that nature.

50
00:02:57,280 --> 00:03:02,560
The scale of the platform is unique in that we touch more than two-thirds of all

51
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:07,159
academic medical centers, more than 55% of all oncologists, 7,000 of which are

52
00:03:07,159 --> 00:03:10,280
regularly ordering our tests and interacting with our products.

53
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:14,879
And the data set we've amassed as a result of that is more than 400 petabytes of

54
00:03:14,879 --> 00:03:17,879
rich, multimodal healthcare data.

55
00:03:17,879 --> 00:03:21,519
When I say multimodal, what I'm referring to is phenotypic morphologic and

56
00:03:21,519 --> 00:03:22,199
molecular data.

57
00:03:22,199 --> 00:03:25,599
So think of it as text, image, and molecules at scale.

58
00:03:25,599 --> 00:03:27,120
So who's this patient?

59
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:28,519
What drugs are they taking?

60
00:03:28,519 --> 00:03:30,079
How are they responding?

61
00:03:30,079 --> 00:03:32,199
And what's their molecular composition?

62
00:03:32,199 --> 00:03:36,680
Understanding all of those, and critically understanding all of those,

63
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:38,840
is necessary to advance AI.

64
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:41,359
Everything else is just a point solution.

65
00:03:41,359 --> 00:03:44,680
It will solve part of the problem, but not solve all the problem.

66
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:48,800
We've been focused on amassing this data set.

67
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:54,800
We had a theory that it was crazy that people would try to do research.

68
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:58,879
Ten years ago when I started Tempest, building these very small and

69
00:03:58,879 --> 00:04:00,599
expensive data sets.

70
00:04:00,599 --> 00:04:07,040
Writing grants, raising money, trying to procure samples in small denominations,

71
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:10,159
sending them off to places like the Broad to be sequenced.

72
00:04:10,159 --> 00:04:12,600
And as a result, you'd amass 50 or

73
00:04:12,639 --> 00:04:16,000
100 patients worth of data over a year or two.

74
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:20,680
And it was crazy to me that at the time people were sequencing patients at scale,

75
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:22,319
