87
00:04:53,439 --> 00:04:55,800
It spans over 45 million patients.

88
00:04:55,800 --> 00:04:59,639
Over 8 million have digitized imaging records that are annotated.

89
00:04:59,639 --> 00:05:02,279
We've sequenced over 4 million samples.

90
00:05:02,279 --> 00:05:06,720
And at the very bottom of this funnel, there's more than 350,000 records

91
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:12,440
that have rich molecular data, rich genomic data, rich transcriptomic data,

92
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:15,080
rich imaging data, rich clinical data.

93
00:05:15,080 --> 00:05:18,840
And that data set really powers the majority of our data business today,

94
00:05:18,840 --> 00:05:19,840
which operates at scale.

95
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:29,120
The idea of marrying these two concepts of taking clinical diagnostics and

96
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:34,120
